From: Stained-Glass-OS-contributors <noreply@stainedglass.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 07:43:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] doctrenderer: build against Debian's V8 (libnode)

In sg_debian mode the JavaScript engine is the V8 Debian ships in libnode
(V8 11.3 with nodejs 20), built without pointer compression or sandbox, in
place of a V8 8.9 built from Chromium's depot_tools. It exports everything
doctrenderer uses, SnapshotCreator included. V8's internal src/base headers
are not part of it, so the memory limits come from sysconf/getrlimit, and
V8 11 disposes its platform with DisposePlatform. The inspector (a websocket
debug server) is left out.
---
 Common/3dParty/v8/v8.pri                      | 142 ++++++++++--------
 .../doctrenderer/js_internal/js_base.pri      |   1 +
 .../doctrenderer/js_internal/v8/v8_base.h     |  30 +++-
 3 files changed, 104 insertions(+), 69 deletions(-)

